#! 0.2.36's argv readers on the wire (tl34): s261's `env_arg0` and
#! `env_args_bytes` ([os.env.argv]), the two prelude functions of the
#! release's seven that a portable document can name. The other five are
#! s263's `VaList` and its four `va_*` builtins, and those are E0826 on
#! every target but x86-64 Linux, at the type's name itself (measured on
#! the acquired darwin binary, docs/PIN-0236.md §2), so a session naming
#! them would diagnose differently on each OS the replay runs on; they are
#! measured on hasu's linux server in docs/PIN-0236.md instead.
#!
#! Three surfaces, the three the contract names, on s261's own witness:
#!
#!   HOVER. 9:15 and 10:15 are the builtin FUNCTION names; `hover-net-wait`
#!   measured that such a name hovers to the type of the CALL it heads,
#!   over the call's range, so `str` and `List[List[byte]]` are expected
#!   over `env_arg0()` and `env_args_bytes()`. 9:8 and 10:8 are the
#!   bindings that take them: the same two types, now through a `let`.
#!
#!   SIGNATURE HELP. 9:24 and 10:30 sit inside the empty argument lists.
#!   `annotate/signatureHelp-*` measured `null` on `print(...)`, a builtin
#!   call, so `null` is expected: the server signs user functions only.
#!
#!   COMPLETION. 9:18 and 10:18 are partway through each name (`env|_arg0`,
#!   `env|_args_bytes`), invoked. `completion-s137` measured the prelude
#!   absent from completion entirely, so neither name is expected among
#!   the items; the whole list is recorded, so the day the prelude reaches
#!   completion this record moves by a knowable amount.
#!
#! Recorded against the acquired 0.2.35 server the same script diagnoses
#! both names E0301 (neither exists there): that is this file's red.
name      requests/hover-argv
profile   minimal

initialize
open      os/arg0.lu
wait      diagnostics os/arg0.lu
req       hover os/arg0.lu 9:15
req       hover os/arg0.lu 10:15
req       hover os/arg0.lu 9:8
req       hover os/arg0.lu 10:8
req       signatureHelp os/arg0.lu 9:24
req       signatureHelp os/arg0.lu 10:30
req       completion os/arg0.lu 9:18
req       completion os/arg0.lu 10:18
shutdown
